    "An angular, 3d art style, with brush stroke color texture. Maximum wide high-angle aerial shot looking straight down from far above, NO camera tilt, the camera has risen to the highest point and pulled away to the widest view, a SINGLE young Indian schoolboy, exactly one kid, one person only, around ten years old, wearing a neat school uniform of a collared shirt tucked into full-length long trousers, NO tie, a red school bag, the boy is a very small tiny dot in the center of the frame, the boy is looking up at the camera, the entire long traditional stone bridge with many arches and the whole river and the vast surrounding environment are visible, the sky and open space dominate the upper portion of the frame with negative space, lush paddy fields and tall coconut palms on both banks, rolling green hills far in the background, warm soft light, vast cinematic depth, highly detailed, no text, no letters, no words, no title, 16:9 widescreen"
   ]
